{
  "reason": "The current residual MultVAE–SASRec ensemble achieves measured macro validation HR@10 of 0.625, while SASRec still uses independent BCE with one negative per active transition. Sampling, training-logit computation, and loss integration must change together to test direct competition against 16 alternatives. Historical success with this objective in a MultVAE ensemble supports the experiment, but failure in a different ensemble shows that gains are uncertain; retain the current residual MultVAE and equal-weight mean-rank fusion.",
  "module": [
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering",
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "Modify sample_batch(user_train, itemnum, batch_size, maxlen) so negatives has shape (batch_size, maxlen, 16), while sequences and positives retain their current shapes and chronological contents. At every active position, draw 16 independent uniform item IDs with replacement from 1 through itemnum, rejecting items in the user's complete training-history set excluded; allow duplicate negatives and leave padded rows zero. Preserve the function signature, variable names, three-array return order, eligible-user selection, and existing no-eligible-negatives guard. Keep Histories, pack_rows, binary-history normalization, validation_batches, supplied seed-0 splits, all four DATASETS, and DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'] unchanged.",
    "model_design": "Update SASRec.forward(self, seq, pos=None, neg=None) to support negatives shaped (batch, maxlen, 16), computing h = self.features(seq) once and selecting active positions with pos.ne(0) before negative embedding lookup. Return positive logits shaped (N_active,) and negative logits shaped (N_active, 16), using unscaled dot products; gathering active positions first limits padding-related memory overhead. Preserve the signature, two-value training return interface, and existing features return when pos is None, updating the training caller for the new output shapes. Keep every parameter, initialization, dimension, dropout setting, features and predict behavior, residual MultVAE architecture and objective, expert_scores, descending_ranks, and equal-weight normalized mean-rank rank_fusion unchanged, avoiding historically unsuccessful reciprocal-rank fusion and unrelated architectural additions.",
    "training_evaluation": "In train_sasrec(name, device, deadline), replace both BCE terms and their obsolete output masking with F.cross_entropy(torch.cat([positive_logits[:, None], negative_logits], dim=1).float(), torch.zeros(positive_logits.shape[0], dtype=torch.long, device=device)), averaging uniformly over active transitions at temperature 1 without sampling corrections or auxiliary objectives. Preserve the existing optional embedding regularization, optimizers, learning rates, batch sizes, STEPS, EPOCHS default 200, seed-42 training streams, validation cadence, HR@10 checkpoint selection with NDCG@10 tie-breaking, patience, member allocations, and single-GPU execution. Add lightweight checks for negative shapes, zero padding, complete-history exclusion, finite cross-entropy, and gradient flow using isolated RNG state; retain checkpoint reload, verify_fusion, and generated-predictor parity checks. Preserve write_predict_script(), saved constructor configurations, inference forward passes, and predict(user_id, history, candidates, *, dataset_name=None), since inference architecture and scoring remain unchanged; retain all four routes and trial-local artifacts while accounting for every consumed trial in the remaining shared 43,200 GPU-second budget. Report measured member and ensemble category metrics and macro validation HR@10 against 0.625, treating the proposed gain as unverified and leaving the pinned host evaluation of 200 validation users per category, 99 unique negative candidates, evaluation seed 42, and hidden-test evaluation unchanged."
  }
}
